{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py` is 796 LOC — 4 under the 800 hard cap enforced by the CI module-size gate (`.github/module-size-limit.txt`), so any addition turns the build red. It grew because a single module accreted THREE distinct responsibilities: the run mechanism, cache-effectiveness *diagnostics*, and *failure interpretation*. Zero in-progress file_impact contention. Flagged by audit ae1b.\n\n## Approach\nDecompose by responsibility (not by line count) into three cohesive modules with a one-way dependency direction — the recurrence-preventing fix: future cache-warning or failure-classification logic then lands in its own module instead of re-inflating the orchestrator.\n\n1. Extract the **cache-effectiveness diagnostics** cluster → new `src/rebar/llm/cache_diagnostics.py` (~230 LOC): `warn_if_cache_ineffective` (structured_run.py:533), `cache_write_never_read` (:645), `warn_if_cache_write_never_read` (:675), `estimate_marked_prefix_tokens` (:704), `_warn_if_zeroed_usage` (:740).\n2. Extract the **failure-interpretation** cluster → new `src/rebar/llm/run_failure.py` (~180 LOC): `FailureContext` (:45), `interpret_failure` (:59), `_write_parse_failure_artifact` (:304).\n3. `structured_run.py` retains the run mechanism (`_pai_structured` :186, `build_model_settings` :342, `build_usage_limits` :420, `effective_max_iterations` :461, `_known_model_output_ceiling` :470, `effective_max_tokens` :489, `_extract_usage` :499, `_import_pydantic_ai` :764, `_pai_check_config` :775) → ~390 LOC.\n\nRationale (G6): responsibility-based seams are stable, so the split does not need to be redone as code evolves; the two extracted modules are pure/observability code with no back-edge into the orchestrator. **Preserve every public import path** by re-exporting the moved names from `structured_run.py` (`from .run_failure import FailureContext, interpret_failure` etc.) — external importers `llm/runner.py`, `llm/usage_report.py`, `llm/capabilities.py` docs, and the tests are then untouched, keeping the edit-set non-overlapping. The re-export also keeps `test_structured_run_seam.py::test_moved_symbols_are_importable_from_the_new_module` (which asserts `hasattr(structured_run, \"_warn_if_zeroed_usage\")`) green with no test edit.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py` — remove the two extracted clusters; add re-export shims.\n- `src/rebar/llm/cache_diagnostics.py` — NEW (cache-effectiveness diagnostics).\n- `src/rebar/llm/run_failure.py` — NEW (failure interpretation + parse-failure artifact).\n\n## Verification (behavior-preserving refactor — no new behavior)\n- Moved code is byte-identical; only imports are adjusted. No test edits.\n- `mypy`, ruff, and the module-size gate stay green; `structured_run.py` ≤ 500 LOC; both new modules ≥ 100 LOC.\n- Existing oracle tests pass unchanged: `tests/unit/test_structured_run_seam.py`, `tests/unit/test_interpret_failure_seam.py`, `tests/unit/test_cache_floor_warning.py`, `tests/unit/test_cache_floor_per_model.py`, `tests/unit/test_cache_prefix_breakpoint.py`, `tests/unit/test_settings_builders_seam.py`, `tests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `wc -l src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py` ≤ 500; each new sibling ≥ 100 LOC.\n- [ ] `cache_diagnostics.py` and `run_failure.py` contain exactly the named symbols; neither imports back from `structured_run.py`, and neither imports `runner` at runtime.\n- [ ] All prior external import paths still resolve (verified: `python -c \"import rebar.llm.structured_run as s; s.interpret_failure; s.FailureContext; s.build_model_settings; s.warn_if_cache_ineffective; s.warn_if_cache_write_never_read; s._warn_if_zeroed_usage; s.estimate_marked_prefix_tokens\"`).\n- [ ] The full default suite and the module-size/complexity/type/lint gates are green with no test edits required."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786597194462682001,"uuid":"c6c53bd6-87d1-424c-8963-a563cf4b389c"}